0.31.0 -> 0.31.1 : New Game BR-02 shipment selector (1-6, default 1); selected robots spawn in six marked depot-side bays, autonomously claim different construction targets for parallel work, share physical resource sources, maintain fleet clearance while moving, and are persisted in save schema 3; schema-2 saves load as a one-robot fleet.
0.31.1 -> 0.31.2 : BR-02 collision/animation pass; robot navigation now uses a chassis-sized pressure-shell envelope, avoids incomplete structure footprints, physical ground pallets, Storage Dome cargo boxes and fleet mates, and uses a wider obstacle-steering fan; pickup, put-down, material application, welding and build-up are explicit timed construction actions with animated manipulator/tool effects, and each construction stage commits only after the full visible work sequence completes.
0.31.3 - Persistent construction ghost meshes; smoother BR-02 steering/arrival; moving work-perimeter construction; refined pickup/place/apply/weld/build animations; flat update-package layout.
0.31.3 -> 0.31.4 : construction-aware robot navigation now collides only with actually revealed/erected mesh so robots can cross unbuilt blueprint volume; added CR-01 dedicated carrier logistics with storage-first supply routing and automatic consolidation of loose resources into completed Storage Domes; BR-02 constructors prioritize on-site assembly and self-haul only when carrier support is unavailable; added NORMAL 1X / QUICK 2X / FAST 4X simulation controls in the bottom bar with save persistence.
0.31.4 -> 0.31.5 : robot anti-entrapment construction gating; each stage now performs a fleet-wide future-mesh safety check and evacuates robots from wall-producing habitat/resource footprints or newly revealed network geometry before committing the step; ordinary navigation still collides only with already constructed mesh. Update archives return to one versioned top-level game-update-vX.Y.Z directory.
0.31.5 -> 0.31.6 : independent New Game selectors for 1-6 BR-02 builders and 1-6 CR-01 carriers; carrier logistics remains dedicated to resource-source/depot-to-site hauling while builders self-haul when a starved site has no effective incoming material; all robot travel now uses precomputed collision-aware shortest paths with line-of-sight smoothing and spatial route reservations, preventing fleet routes from intersecting and serializing traffic through narrow passages.
0.31.6 -> 0.31.7 : cooperative construction crews; multiple BR-02 builders and CR-01 carriers may work the same construction target through one shared site buffer/coordinator, carrier deliveries are capacity-reserved to prevent duplicate hauling, builder work is distributed around the target and accelerates moderately with crew size, and CR-01 transit speed is normalized to exactly 110% of BR-02 speed (2.42 m/s vs 2.20 m/s), including older saves.
0.31.7 -> 0.31.8 : CR-01 carrier logistics rebuilt around an explicit per-site required/delivered/reserved/unassigned material ledger; every transport trip reserves an exact material mass before travel, builders only self-haul unreserved shortages, ground-pallet service points and starter-depot spacing guarantee physical pickup access, and homogeneous material trips eliminate multi-stack pickup deadlocks. Every BR-02/CR-01 is individually world-selectable with live status, condition, cargo, route, target and site-ledger inspection. Save schema 5 persists condition/reservations with backward compatibility.
0.31.9 - Persistent construction status frames for every incomplete build object, with remaining resource demand and progress bars.
