0.31.10 -> 0.31.11 : construction-site resource deliveries remain visible as staged material boxes until consumed; robot routes are independent and no longer hard-reserved by another robot, with soft path separation and short-horizon reciprocal collision avoidance to prevent fleet deadlocks/stuttering; construction progress frames explicitly use the global UI-scale transform.
0.31.11 -> 0.31.12 : construction rendering is blueprint-only for every incomplete habitat/resource structure/corridor/supply channel/walkway; no filled/material surfaces are emitted before completion, unbuilt geometry is subdued blue, and erected geometry uses brighter substantially thicker blue wireframe lines.
0.31.12 -> 0.31.13 : robot-runtime stabilization; game-speed-independent critically damped robot rendering, stable per-task pickup/delivery/build stations, coarse-grid A* final stand-off connectors and non-orbiting waypoint handling, persistent per-robot recovery service slots, footprint-aware cooperative builder crew limits, local watchdog recovery without fleet-wide waiting, and corrected construction anti-entrapment sequencing that evaluates only newly revealed mesh and evacuates robots to wider exterior safety points before stage commit. Delivered site-buffer resources remain visible as staged boxes and individual robot selection continues to expose task/status, cargo and condition.
0.31.13 -> 0.31.14 : coordinated pre-motion robot route reservations with visible ground routes and deterministic waiting/replanning; builders use fixed construction service stations instead of orbiting/spinning; construction visuals restored as full blue target meshes with progressively replaced yellow installed geometry and bold green completed meshes for habitats, facilities, corridors, supply channels and walkways; construction frames show explicit stage progress.

0.31.14 -> 0.31.15 : hard rendered-hull robot separation with collision-tested turning and post-step overlap repair; co-directional shared routes can operate as spaced convoy lanes while crossing/opposing routes retain right-of-way reservations; CR-01 carriers pre-stage the full remaining construction material backlog, immediately clear completed trip state, and continue accepting follow-up transport work instead of stalling after the first delivery.
0.31.15 -> 0.31.16 : robot autonomy/navigation rewrite; removed reactive steering-fan/retreat motion and replaced it with precomputed spatial A* plus time-expanded cooperative reservation slots inspired by Cooperative A*/SIPP, including explicit planned waits for crossing traffic, swept hull-conflict checks, deterministic fixed-slot execution, and hard no-overlap runtime guards; pickup/construction/Storage Dome service stations now choose hull-safe fleet-separated positions so carriers are never assigned physically impossible destinations; route inspector/ground visualization exposes cooperative travel/hold slots.
0.31.16 -> 0.31.17 : continuous multi-robot traffic overhaul; removed 0.48-second cooperative stop/go slots and render-spring catch-up, replacing them with Theta*-style any-angle route planning, rounded/densified waypoints, full-route fleet trajectory preflight, traffic-weighted alternate lanes, PIBT-inspired dynamic right-of-way aging, continuous reciprocal speed governing and deterministic replan-on-yield without reactive steering/spinning; robot simulation substeps increased to 90 Hz with no dropped FAST-mode remainder; all construction objects are mesh-only with no structure surfaces/textures, retaining blue blueprint / yellow installed / bold green completed wireframes.
0.31.17 -> 0.31.18 : construction-placement and fleet-scheduling stabilization; replaced full-map multi-pass route rasterization with cached corridor-local A* that widens only for required detours, split route-plan budgets between constructors and carriers, rebuilt the starter depot into hull-safe parking plus deterministic material entry/pickup/exit lanes, serialized only same-source pickup traffic, returned idle carriers to clear standby bays, made normal logistics carrier-first with delayed coordinator-only builder fallback, fixed operation stations for each trip, and kept loaded logistics reservations authoritative while blocked. QA covers live second-structure placement with 6 builders + 6 carriers and placement scaling across 16/64/128/256/512 playfields.
0.31.18 -> 0.31.19 : concurrent logistics-lane refinement; BR-02 work stations now follow the actual rotated structure perimeter with ~0.20 m front tool clearance, construction and Storage Dome service positions are hull-reserved before travel, starter-depot same-material trips use a stable staged queue with one-way outer-gate -> lane -> pallet flow and a clear loaded-rover exit, source reservations may queue without double-counting physical stock, fleet prediction integrates actual speed/acceleration rather than assuming instant cruise, carrier site selection balances concurrent construction demand, and any active builder may claim the single stage commit so a delayed original site owner cannot freeze construction. QA places two structures simultaneously with 6 builders + 6 carriers and verifies parallel deliveries/building with zero hull collisions.
0.31.19 -> 0.31.20 : construction logistics handoff overhaul; every site now uses one deterministic visible material drop zone, CR-01s queue/stage/exit around that single apron, BR-02 fallback hauling covers only uncovered stage demand and uses the same drop queue, builders physically collect the current stage bundle from the drop before assembly, every build step is worked from all four structure sides via planned perimeter/corner waypoints, future construction geometry is reserved before segments appear so robots cannot occupy the next-step volume, and carrier depot ownership/queue ageing is stabilized to prevent lane deadlocks during ongoing construction.
